Subject: [PATCH 06846/11362] ARC round-3 (codex): sp80 honest null, L6
 whole-level budget found

First result of the round-3 breadth campaign against the 15 remaining
unsolved games. sp80's L6 wall holds: tested four rendered-geometry
routing families (centered/shifted embedded-source splitters, both elbow
orientations, a target-aligned vertical splitter) -- none won.

Genuinely new finding despite the null: L6 has a FINITE WHOLE-LEVEL
action budget, not merely the previously-documented per-commit
border-pixel counter -- after 79 exploratory suffix actions, an ordinary
movement action ended the episode with an empty terminal frame. This
narrows the search for a future attempt (route planning must respect a
hard action ceiling on top of the per-commit counter).

No new level banked; reproducible_total_levels stays 138.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
